// SPILL PRESSURE: locals past the register band, and calls above them.
//
// Locals past ZYM_LOCAL_REG_CAP (192) spill to the per-frame spill stack,
// which lives OFF the value stack. A callee's frame is based just above
// the caller's registers and grows upward -- exactly where an in-frame
// spill area sat -- so before this, 252 locals plus any call silently read
// back the CALLEE's locals. Every assertion here pins that shape.
//
// Everything above the highest live local stays available to temps and
// call windows, which is what keeps calls working in local-heavy code.
//
// NOTE ON ZYM_FORCE_SPILL_AT: unlike spill.zym, this file is a
// DEFAULT-MODE test. The debug knob sets temp_alloc_cap = N + 4, so at
// N=8 the entire temp band is 4 registers -- not enough for a 2-arg call
// whose accumulator must first be SPILL_LOADed (1 scratch + a 3-slot call
// window). That is a property of the knob's tiny window, not of spilling.
// spill.zym covers the forced-spill path; this one covers the real band.
//
// Uses the native assert(), which raises, so a regression stops the file.

func callee() { var a = 601
 var b = 602
 var c = 603
 return 600 }

